{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And unto Shem were also born children</b> — because after recounting the generations of Shem he recounted the generations of his brother who is younger than he, as though he had no children, therefore it says here \"also he.\"" "And the meaning of <b>the father of all the children of Eber</b> is that he is the father of all the dwellers across the River (ever ha-nahar), which is the place of Abraham's lineage. And it is not possible that \"Eber\" in this place be the name of the man who was the father of Peleg, for why would he trace them back to him?" "<b>the brother of Japheth the great</b> — the way of Scripture is to trace the younger to the elder among brothers, and not to the one born after him. And so too, \"Miriam the prophetess, the sister of Aaron\" (Exodus 15:20). And the reason for mentioning this at all is to say that he is the brother of the honored one, equal to him in honor, to make known that he did not delay him on account of Ham's superiority over him. And it appears to me that \"the great\" (הגדול) is an epithet for Shem, to say that he is the great brother of Japheth, for Ham is the youngest of them all, yet he placed him first. And so in every place, an epithet applies to the one being spoken of, as in \"Isaiah the son of Amoz the prophet\" (II Kings 20:1), \"Hananiah the son of Azur the prophet\" (Jeremiah 28:1), \"Hobab the son of Reuel the Midianite, Moses' father-in-law\" (Numbers 10:29). And Rashi wrote (Rashi on Genesis 10:21): \"the brother of Japheth\" and not the brother of Ham, for those two honored their father while this one disgraced him. Also, this is to say that he is the brother of the righteous one and not the brother of the wicked one, even though he is listed after him."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {1 "The parenthetical citation כ״פ הרד״ק והראב״ע שמות כא ב appears to reference the position of Radak and Ibn Ezra that עבר (Eber) means 'the region across the river'; the Exodus 21:2 reference is obscure in this context and may be a textual corruption or misplaced citation."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:27:25.251451121Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}